BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 619.0 Tm (1. A patient has a sudden rise in arteriolar sympathetic firing with minimal change in cardiac output. Which) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 605.3 Tm (immediate variable rises most directly?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 588.6 Tm (Answer: C. Total peripheral resistance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 572.3 Tm (Explanation: Arteriolar constriction increases resistance and therefore tends to raise arterial pressure even at) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 559.2 Tm (stable output.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 543.1 Tm (Not A: SA nodal rate concerns cardiac autonomic effects rather than arteriolar action.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 529.7 Tm (Not B: Metabolite clearance depends on local blood flow, not this direct action.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 516.3 Tm (Not D: Sympathetic venoconstriction generally reduces venous compliance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 502.9 Tm (Source: circulation-2:Q27 | 3, 13, 19, 21) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 479.7 Tm (2. The R-R separation is four large squares on a regular standard-speed ECG. What is the heart rate?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 463.0 Tm (Answer: A. 75 beats/min.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 446.7 Tm (Explanation: At 25 mm/s, a large square equals 0.20 s. Four large squares represent 0.8 s per beat, giving 60/0.8 = 75) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 433.6 Tm (beats/min.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 417.5 Tm (Not B: 120 beats/min would require 2.5 large squares.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 404.1 Tm (Not C: 60 beats/min would require five large squares between R waves.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 390.7 Tm (Not D: 90 beats/min would require about 3.33 large squares.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 377.3 Tm (Source: lecture-7:Q42 | 13-14) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 354.1 Tm (3. Portal hypertension promotes ascites partly by increasing which force?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 337.4 Tm (Answer: B. Hydrostatic pressure in hepatic sinusoids.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 321.1 Tm (Explanation: Higher sinusoidal hydrostatic pressure increases fluid filtration and hepatic lymph formation; excess) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 308.0 Tm (can enter the peritoneal cavity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 291.9 Tm (Not A: Higher plasma oncotic pressure would oppose outward fluid filtration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 278.5 Tm (Not C: Improved lymphatic clearance would tend to oppose accumulation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 265.1 Tm (Not D: Oxygen tension is not the main Starling-force mechanism.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 251.7 Tm (Source: lecture-6:Q44 | 37) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 228.5 Tm (4. Which contrast best distinguishes forward failure from backward failure?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 211.8 Tm (Answer: A. Forward reduces delivery; backward causes venous congestion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 195.5 Tm (Explanation: Forward failure describes inadequate delivery to downstream tissues, whereas backward failure) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 182.4 Tm (describes elevated pressure and congestion upstream of a failing chamber.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 166.3 Tm (Not B: The two effects are reversed in this statement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 152.9 Tm (Not C: Reduced flow and congestion, not excessive output, are the defining patterns.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 139.5 Tm (Not D: Either side can produce both forward and backward consequences.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 126.1 Tm (Source: circulation-3:Q48 | Circulation 3, slides 32-33) Tj ET
